\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. We thank Thee, Lord, for this fair earth,
\par The glittering sky, the silver sea;
\par For all their beauty, all their worth,
\par Their light and glory, come from Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thanks for the flowers that clothe the ground,
\par The trees that wave their arms above,
\par The hills that gird our dwellings round,
\par As Thou dost gird Thine own with love.
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par \'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Yet teach us still how far more fair,
\par More glorious, Father, in Thy sight,
\par Is one pure deed, one holy prayer,
\par One heart that owns Thy Spirit's might.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. So, while we gaze with thoughtful eye
\par On all the gifts Thy Love has given,
\par Help us in Thee to live and die,
\par By Thee to rise from earth to heaven.
\par                                        Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

